From: MiaAI_Lab <mia.ailab1@gmail.com>
Subject: server: a call after prose that quotes its opener is the call, not content

A reply whose prose names tool-call markup ("each lab's format differs: <minimax:tool_call>, Qwen's <tool_call>{}")
and then makes a call in GLM's markup came back as content with no tool_calls, and the agent's turn ended there.
tool_parse.envelopes takes the earliest <tool_call> and the first </tool_call> after it, so the quoted opener began
the envelope, the call did not parse as its payload (GLM's name held the quoted text), and the envelope was kept as
content: "warning: kept 1 malformed or unoffered tool envelopes as content" in the rank log, 1 of 203 requests on
2026-11-04 and 7 of 834 on 2026-11-03 on this pair.

parse now retries a rejected <tool_call> envelope from the last opener inside it, and up to four openers back from
there for a value that quotes the opener itself; the text before the opener that parses stays content. A call that
still does not parse whole, or names a tool the request did not offer, stays content as before, and a reply of many
quoted openers is rejected in linear time. closeCall parses the closed text the same way, so it now closes such a
call that the end token left open; the test that recorded an earlier opener taking the closer moves into the new
test as a positive case. A streamed reply still hides the prose from the quoted opener on and sends it with the
final chunk, as it did when the envelope was rejected.

Found and fixed by Mia's AI Lab on this pair; the streamer (tool_stream.zig) is unchanged: it already gives up on
GLM's markup and leaves the calls to this final parse.

